From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64: heartbeat and stall watch on the serial console

Diagnostic for #14 and #157: every 60 s each CPU writes [hb <cpu> <n> s..
w.. i.. p..] straight to the PL011, without the COM1 lock, and each CPU
reports once when another CPU takes no timer interrupt ([hb stall]) or
runs no schedule() ([hb nosched]) for 2 s.
---
diff -ruN a/src/arch/aarch64/device/generic_timer.rs b/src/arch/aarch64/device/generic_timer.rs
--- a/src/arch/aarch64/device/generic_timer.rs
+++ b/src/arch/aarch64/device/generic_timer.rs
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+use core::sync::atomic::{AtomicU32, Ordering};
 use spin::Once;
 
 use super::{cpu::registers::control_regs, ic_for_chip, irqchip};
@@ -193,6 +194,134 @@
